--- HOW TO USE, and why it is a patch file and not shipped source ---

Apply with:   git apply shots/r24-clauseC-probe.patch
Then:         npm run build -- --outDir dist-rX
              node shots/_massdrive.mjs --base http://HOST/custom_robot/?chamfer=0.35 \
                   --arena grid --tier 3 --seed 1234567 --onbody

Knobs, all defaulting to the shipped behaviour so a URL without them reproduces
head to the third decimal (verified: control 1.706 / 1.287 against head 1.705 /
1.288, top4 85.3 / 86.2 against RULING 18's filed 85.3 / 86.2):

    ?chamfer=k    scales every roundedBox corner radius
    ?plane=k      scales PLANE_UP / PLANE_DOWN
    ?grime=k      scales the bottom-to-top baked value ramp, toward FLAT AND
                  FULL VALUE (k=0 puts every vertex at 1.0), never toward dark
    ?plateau=1    replaces the continuous ny*ny plane ramp with three hard
                  levels — top plate, side plate, underside

It is NOT shipped source. A query-string switch read by the renderer and by
nothing else is the `ssao` fault waiting to happen: a later round would probe
it, read "not the cause", and never learn that it was "not present". Round 24
measured all four to exhaustion (see REVIEW2, round 24) and every one of them
is closed, so the code has no reason to exist in the build and every reason to
exist here.
